@startuml direct-rialto-trickplay-activity
title Trick-play: effect of Flush(position, rate != 1)

start
:AAMP: TeardownStream -> Flush(0, rate) placeholder\n-> Configure() -> Flush(position, rate) -> Stream();
:Flush stages rate; m_rate committed on SEEK_DONE\n(or immediately on early-exit paths);
:ArmPreRoll(rate): pre-roll disabled for rate != 1\n-> ReleaseHold(PreRollIncomplete);
:ResetSourcesForFlush;
if (audio-only content (audio is primary)?) then (yes)
  :subtitle source EOS;\naudio stays live;
else (no)
  :audio and subtitle sources EOS\n(Rialto must not wait for them);
endif
:setPosition(position);
:SEEK_DONE on the Rialto event thread;
if (Rialto isVideoMaster() == false?) then (yes)
  :appliedRate = rate;\nvideo setSourcePosition(pos,\nresetTime=false, appliedRate);
else (no)
  :appliedRate = 1.0 (no extra call);
endif
:play() (no pre-roll);
:GetPositionMilliseconds:\n(Rialto position - segment-start baseline) x m_rate\n(clamped at 0 only for forward rates);
:next Flush at rate 1 clears audio/subtitle EOS;
stop
note right
  Playback speed (SetPlayBackRate, latency
  correction) is separate: it calls Rialto
  setPlaybackRate() directly with no flush.
end note
@enduml
